.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt KVM-LIST 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kvm-list
.Nd list the virtual machines on this host with their state, size and disk
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints a line for every machine libvirt knows on this host, running or
not, with the columns:
.Bl -tag -width "ZVOL USED"
.It Li NAME
The libvirt name.
.It Li STATE
As libvirt reports it:
.Ql running ,
.Ql paused ,
.Ql shut off
and so on.
.It Li RAM
The machine's maximum memory, in MiB (written MB).
.It Li VCPUS
Its virtual processors.
.It Li ZVOL USED
The space its disk,
.Pa rpool/vms/ Ns Ar name ,
takes in the pool: what it holds, not its size.
.Ql n/a
when the machine's disk is not there \(em a machine made by hand, or
whose disk is a file or lives in another dataset.
.El
.Pp
Below the table is the space used by, and available to,
.Pa rpool/vms
as a whole.
.Pp
Machines are listed in libvirt's order, running ones first.
.Pp
.Nm
must run as root; run as a user it re-executes itself with
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Fl -help
needs neither.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
The machines were listed, or there are none.
.It 1
libvirt could not be asked.
.It 2
An argument was given.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed by
.Nm
on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-29.
.Ss Every machine
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kvm-list
NAME                 STATE        RAM        VCPUS  ZVOL USED
app-adguard-ho       shut off     1024MB     1      713M
app-icecast-st       shut off     4096MB     8      1.41G
\&...
klab-blue-centos     shut off     384MB      1      5.70M
klab-blue-debian     shut off     384MB      1      n/a
\&...
klab-golden-centos   shut off     4096MB     2      2.41G
\&...
vdi                  shut off     2048MB     2      8K
vdi-1                shut off     2048MB     2      2.01G
web-golden           shut off     2048MB     2      1.92G

ZFS pool space:
NAME        USED  AVAIL
rpool/vms  74.7G   170G
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
.Ql klab-blue-centos
is a clone of
.Ql klab-golden-centos Ns @golden :
its 5.70M is what it has written since, the rest is shared
with its golden.
.Ql klab-blue-debian
has no disk under
.Pa rpool/vms .
.Ss Arguments are not a filter
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kvm-list web01
kvm-list: takes no arguments (got: web01); try kvm-list --help
# (exited 2)
.Ed
.Pp
To pick machines out, filter the output:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kvm-list | grep -E '^(NAME|klab-golden)'
NAME                 STATE        RAM        VCPUS  ZVOL USED
klab-golden-centos   shut off     4096MB     2      2.41G
klab-golden-debian   shut off     4096MB     2      1.14G
klab-golden-fedora   shut off     4096MB     2      2.27G
klab-golden-rocky    shut off     4096MB     2      2.34G
klab-golden-ubuntu   shut off     4096MB     2      1.25G
NAME        USED  AVAIL
.Ed
.Pp
The last line is the pool summary's header, which the pattern also
matches.
.Ss When libvirt does not answer
Here pointed at a socket that does not exist:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# LIBVIRT_DEFAULT_URI='qemu+unix:///system?socket=/nonexistent' kvm-list
error: failed to connect to the hypervisor
error: Failed to connect socket to '/nonexistent': No such file or directory
kvm-list: could not ask libvirt for its machines (see above)
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "kvm-list: could not ask libvirt for its machines (see above)"
.Xr virsh 1
could not reach libvirt; its own error is printed above.
.It "kvm-list: takes no arguments (got: ARGS); try kvm-list --help"
There are no options or filters.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kld 1 ,
.Xr virsh 1 ,
.Xr kvm-clone 8 ,
.Xr kvm-create 8 ,
.Xr kvm-delete 8 ,
.Xr kvm-snap 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-29, writing this page: with libvirt unreachable the table
printed its header and no rows and exited 0, the same as a host with no
machines; arguments were ignored, so
.Ql kvm-list web01
listed everything; and names longer than 20 characters pushed their rows
out of line.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Only the disk at
.Pa rpool/vms/ Ns Ar name
is measured.
A machine's data disk,
.Ar name Ns Pa -data ,
is not; its space appears only in the pool total.
